---
// Where KrakenKey sits next to common stacks: three places the key can live,
// what serves the certificate in each, and probes checking the live result.
---

<figure class="kk-diagram">
  <div class="kk-scroll">
  <svg viewBox="0 0 760 500" role="img" aria-labelledby="arch-title arch-desc">
    <title id="arch-title">KrakenKey reference architecture</title>
    <desc id="arch-desc">
      KrakenKey exchanges CSRs and certificates with three kinds of client. On the host: a Linux server runs the
      KrakenKey CLI on a timer and serves the certificate from nginx, HAProxy or Caddy. In a key vault: Azure Key
      Vault creates the CSR, and App Service or Container Apps serve the merged certificate. In a pipeline: a
      GitHub Actions workflow or scheduled job renews the certificate and deploys it to servers over SSH or imports
      it into AWS Certificate Manager for load balancers and CloudFront. Probes, hosted by KrakenKey or running on
      your network, scan what each endpoint actually serves and report back to KrakenKey.
    </desc>
    <defs>
      <marker id="arch-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
        <path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" class="kk-arrowhead"></path>
      </marker>
    </defs>

    <!-- KrakenKey -->
    <rect class="kk-box kk-ours" x="10" y="40" width="150" height="320" rx="10"></rect>
    <text class="kk-title" x="85" y="180" text-anchor="middle">KrakenKey</text>
    <text class="kk-note" x="85" y="204" text-anchor="middle">Issues, renews,</text>
    <text class="kk-note" x="85" y="222" text-anchor="middle">stores certificates</text>

    <!-- Column headings -->
    <text class="kk-heading" x="350" y="24" text-anchor="middle">Where the private key lives</text>
    <text class="kk-heading" x="630" y="24" text-anchor="middle">What serves TLS</text>

    <!-- Lane A: on the host -->
    <rect class="kk-box kk-yours" x="240" y="40" width="220" height="90" rx="10"></rect>
    <text class="kk-tag" x="254" y="62">ON THE HOST</text>
    <text class="kk-title" x="254" y="88">Linux server</text>
    <text class="kk-note" x="254" y="110">CLI + systemd timer</text>
    <rect class="kk-box" x="520" y="40" width="230" height="90" rx="10"></rect>
    <text class="kk-title" x="535" y="78">nginx, HAProxy, Caddy</text>
    <text class="kk-note" x="535" y="100">reads the files, reloads</text>

    <!-- Lane B: key vault -->
    <rect class="kk-box kk-yours" x="240" y="155" width="220" height="90" rx="10"></rect>
    <text class="kk-tag" x="254" y="177">IN A KEY VAULT</text>
    <text class="kk-title" x="254" y="203">Azure Key Vault</text>
    <text class="kk-note" x="254" y="225">makes the CSR, merges cert</text>
    <rect class="kk-box" x="520" y="155" width="230" height="90" rx="10"></rect>
    <text class="kk-title" x="535" y="193">App Service,</text>
    <text class="kk-title" x="535" y="215">Container Apps</text>

    <!-- Lane C: pipeline -->
    <rect class="kk-box kk-yours" x="240" y="270" width="220" height="90" rx="10"></rect>
    <text class="kk-tag" x="254" y="292">IN A PIPELINE</text>
    <text class="kk-title" x="254" y="318">GitHub Actions</text>
    <text class="kk-note" x="254" y="340">or any scheduled job</text>
    <rect class="kk-box" x="520" y="270" width="230" height="90" rx="10"></rect>
    <text class="kk-title" x="535" y="300">Servers over SSH</text>
    <text class="kk-title" x="535" y="324">AWS ACM</text>
    <text class="kk-note" x="535" y="344">to ALB, CloudFront</text>

    <!-- KrakenKey <-> clients: CSR in, cert out -->
    <line class="kk-line" x1="162" y1="85" x2="238" y2="85" marker-start="url(#arch-arrow)" marker-end="url(#arch-arrow)"></line>
    <line class="kk-line" x1="162" y1="200" x2="238" y2="200" marker-start="url(#arch-arrow)" marker-end="url(#arch-arrow)"></line>
    <line class="kk-line" x1="162" y1="315" x2="238" y2="315" marker-start="url(#arch-arrow)" marker-end="url(#arch-arrow)"></line>
    <text class="kk-label" x="200" y="75" text-anchor="middle">CSR / cert</text>
    <text class="kk-label" x="200" y="190" text-anchor="middle">CSR / cert</text>
    <text class="kk-label" x="200" y="305" text-anchor="middle">CSR / cert</text>

    <!-- client -> terminator -->
    <line class="kk-line" x1="460" y1="85" x2="518" y2="85" marker-end="url(#arch-arrow)"></line>
    <line class="kk-line" x1="460" y1="200" x2="518" y2="200" marker-end="url(#arch-arrow)"></line>
    <line class="kk-line" x1="460" y1="315" x2="518" y2="315" marker-end="url(#arch-arrow)"></line>

    <!-- Probes -->
    <rect class="kk-box kk-probe" x="240" y="410" width="510" height="76" rx="10"></rect>
    <text class="kk-title" x="495" y="440" text-anchor="middle">Probes: hosted by KrakenKey or on your network</text>
    <text class="kk-note" x="495" y="464" text-anchor="middle">scan what each endpoint really serves: expiry, chain, hostname</text>
    <line class="kk-line kk-dashed" x1="635" y1="408" x2="635" y2="362" marker-end="url(#arch-arrow)"></line>
    <text class="kk-label" x="645" y="392">scan</text>
    <path class="kk-line kk-dashed" d="M240,448 L85,448 L85,362" fill="none" marker-end="url(#arch-arrow)"></path>
    <text class="kk-label" x="100" y="438">results</text>
  </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption>
    Pick one lane per certificate. The probes don't care how a certificate got there, so they also catch hosts that never picked up a renewal.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
